WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
Leave a metal spoon and a plastic
spoon standing in a mug of

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.830
hot tea.

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.290
A minute later, grab the handles.

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.890
The plastic one feels barely warm.

5
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.930
The metal one is too
hot to hold for long.

6
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.910
Both were in the same
tea for the same time.

7
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.110
So how did the thermal
energy reach your fingers?

8
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.190
In this mission, you'll meet
the three ways thermal energy

9
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.820
moves: conduction,
convection and radiation.

10
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.730
You'll see why some surfaces
absorb and give out radiation

11
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.030
better than others, and match
each transfer to everyday

12
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.590
situations.

13
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.410
Your mission: find out how
thermal energy travels.
